  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A PhysBone system on a bone chain where any Parent and Child bone share the same location, or even close locations (roughly within a few centimeters), fail to simulate correctly. The PhysBone system does not know which direction to point the bone, and instead rotates it wildly in many different directions each frame. This effect can be reduced by moving the parent and child bone away from each other, but if they are close, they will still freak out at certain rotations, especially when grabbed.\n\nIn the attached gif, the model on the left of is using a set up where there are child bones that share the same location as their parent bones. The resulting PhysBone simulation error can be observed. On the right, I have moved the child bones slightly away from their roots, and the Physbone simulation is operating correctly.",
